==Battleground==
*2 [[Croakley]]s spawn after 0.07 seconds<sup>2f</sup>, delay 1.67~5 seconds<sup>50f~150f</sup>.
*2 [[Croakley]]s spawn after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>, delay 33.33 seconds<sup>1,000f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Znache]]s spawn after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>, delay 26.67 seconds<sup>800f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Ginger Snache]]s spawn after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>, delay 23.33 seconds<sup>700f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 70% HP:
**1 [[One Horn]] spawns as the boss.
**1 [[Znache]] spawns.
**2 [[Ginger Snache]]s spawn, delay 2.67 seconds<sup>80f</sup>.

==Strategy==
At the beginning send out units to halt the progression of the Croakleys. [[Wushu Cat (Rare Cat)|Shigong Cat]] works surprisingly well for this due to his slow immunity and relatively high DPS for his spammability; plus, he can kill the Znaches easily, another decent option if one lacks Shigong cat could be [[Rover Cat (Rare Cat)|Rover Cat]] if used in its true form, Catellite, in which he gains slow immunity, Once One Horn comes out, kill him as fast as possible with any high DPS units such as [[Swordsman Cat (Rare Cat)|Elemental Duelist Cat]] or [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]]. Nukers such as [[Tropical Kalisa (Uber Rare Cat)|Tropical Kalisa]] can also work if you time them right.

